sdk_examples:
Javascript example (pseudo): 
const resp = await redwood.models.generate({
  model: 'gptx',
  anchor: 'semver:~2.3', // prefer 2.3.x releases
  require_deterministic: true
});
console.log(resp.resolved_ref) // 'gptx@2.3.8-commit-9a1b'

Python example: 
client.generate(model='gptx', anchor='hash:9a1b');

Notes: SDKs should validate the selector syntax locally and surface helpful errors before the network call. When the SDK receives a fallback_chain it should include that in telemetry events for customer observability.
